    "content": "Niele Ivey is the Karen & Kevin Keyes Family Head Women's Basketball Coach at Notre Dame, a position she has held since 2020. A former standout Irish point guard and 2001 NCAA champion, she succeeded Hall of Fame coach Muffet McGraw and has led the team to multiple Sweet Sixteen appearances. This video provides an interview with Coach Niele Ivey about her experience and excitement for the upcoming season:57sIrish Breakdown - Notre Dame FootballYouTube• Oct 24, 2025 57s Key Details About Coach Niele Ivey: Background: Ivey played for Notre Dame from 1996–2001, helping the team win its first national championship. She also played in the WNBA. Coaching Career: Prior to becoming head coach, she served as an assistant coach at Notre Dame (2007–2019) and in the NBA with the Memphis Grizzlies. Achievements: As head coach, she has led the Fighting Irish to consistent success, including fourth consecutive Sweet Sixteen appearances, as noted in this Facebook video. Philosophy: Known as a \"players' coach,\" Ivey emphasizes mentorship and strong relationships, particularly with stars like Hannah Hidalgo, as discussed in this YouTube video. Staff: Carol Owens serves as the Associate Head Coach, according to Notre Dame Athletics. You can watch a postgame press conference with Coach Ivey and her players, where they discuss their team's performance:1mNotre Dame Fighting IrishYouTube• Mar 21, 2026 1m",
